content.thinking:
Now I can see the FloorPosition calculation in ArcCreate:

```csharp
public double GetFloorPosition(int timing)
{
    TimingEvent note = GetEventAt(timing);
    double baseFloorPosition = note.FloorPosition;
    return baseFloorPosition + ((double)note.Bpm * (timing - note.Timing));
}
```

And `FloorPositionToZ`:
```csharp
public static float FloorPositionToZ(double fp, float dropRate) => (float)(fp / Values.BaseBpm * dropRate / -1000);


```

So the floor position accumulates raw BPM without dividing by BaseBpm, then the Z conversion applies that division. This matches our implementation, but I need to understand where TimingPointDensity comes into play and what the precomputed base floor position actually represents for each timing event.

